# Navigator long body drag retains coverage purpose

## Pre-work plan

- Context: Renderer/Interactive.Client 0.2.57 introduced `TaCoverageWindowPurpose` and `ta-coverage-window.v2`. Daedilus installed the immutable packages and proved the first resize and middle move settle correctly, without the retired count heuristic.
- 目標: preserve typed navigator origin and the frozen target range through the post-settlement long body drag, then produce an immutable 0.2.58 owner package for real 18884 verification.
- 假設: the cross-axis-only predicate is the earliest authority loss; axis equality after accepted materialization erases `NavigatorWindow` even though the action still originates from the inner navigator.
- Observed failure: after resize to 79 and a settled middle move, a body drag from resident-local start 1201 to target start 0 emits only `VisibleRangeChanged`; `CoverageIntent` is absent. Consumer settles active 49646 -> 49567 and resident-local 1201 -> 1122 instead of materializing target local 0.
- Source of truth: the pointerdown-frozen navigator domain/window and the emitted action wire captured in `G:\coldfar_py\coldfar-symbolics\temp\agent.daedilus\resident-width-and-edges-0257-bundle\left-edge-80-*.json`, plus the typed `TaCoverageWindowPurpose` contract.
- Invariant: every navigator-origin event-range materialization retains `Purpose=NavigatorWindow` and the exact frozen target event range; main-plot pan remains `MainPlotPan`; no count-based inference returns.
- Scope/owner: producer source/tests/packages under this repository only. Daedilus owns consumer/18884 changes and real-browser acceptance.
- Plan: establish a focused RED for the post-settlement same-axis/long-body-drag path; locate the earliest branch that drops the navigator intent; make the smallest producer fix; run focused/full tests, package verification, package-only consumer build, sensitive/encoding/check gates; commit/push and hand off immutable package evidence.
- Acceptance: resize 1500 -> 79, middle move, then long body drag to local 0 emits a navigator-purpose intent and exact target range; existing main-pan, resident, highlight, and D behavior remain green; Daedilus confirms real 18884 A/B/C and regression gates.
- Risks: same-axis navigation previously relied on a bare `VisibleRangeChanged`; adding the explicit discriminator must not invent an ordinal or change main-plot semantics.

